{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"gassy-porcine-hound","creation_channel":"python","description":"## Context / Problem\n\nAdding the `[code_review]` section re-export in ticket `unaroused-undead-ibisbill` took\n`src/rebar/config.py` from 799 to exactly 800 lines. The CI module-size gate fails on\n`loc > cap` with cap 800 (`.github/module-size-limit.txt`), so the file passes today but the\nNEXT line added to it — a new section class re-export, a new owned accessor — fails CI, and the\nlimit is locked so it cannot be raised by a contributor.\n\n## Approach\n\nSplit `src/rebar/config.py` along an existing call-graph seam, the same way `_config_schema.py`\nand `_config_sources.py` were already carved out of it, so the facade regains headroom without\nchanging any public import path (`from rebar.config import X` must keep working — the module\nalready re-exports every moved name).\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/config.py` — extract one cohesive cluster into a sibling private module.\n- the new sibling module.\n- tests covering the moved surface, if any assert on the old location.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `src/rebar/config.py` is at most 700 lines (`wc -l`), leaving headroom under the 800 cap.\n- [ ] Every name importable from `rebar.config` before the split is still importable after —\n      verified by the existing config test suite passing unchanged.\n- [ ] `make lint` and `make typecheck` exit 0.","id":"0924-f271-d664-4378","parent_id":"546f-cc0f-66e7-4a5a","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"task","title":"src/rebar/config.py sits at the 800-line module-size cap with zero headroom"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788157470617673001,"uuid":"0a0ee1d3-0811-4869-bed9-55a91e77391e"}